#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD0089 expect=violation domain=TE
#note "TEENRL is not present in the dataset, so the wave E Requirements.Variables.All [TEENRL, TEDUR] leg is unmet and the parent SKIPS. Added by the terminal review (finding F-5): the suite pinned only the TEDUR-absent half of a gate that is symmetric in the YAML, so widening it back toward Any on TEENRL alone would have reddened nothing here. The finding is NOT lost: this dataset is byte-for-byte the R-5.25 split sibling FDA-SD0089-B's -violation_tedur_blank scenario, which reports row 2 at its location. Four disjoint states: both present -> parent; one absent -> that column's sibling; neither -> the dataset sister."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset TE label="Trial Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col TESTRL  type=Char label="Rule for Start of Element"
col TEDUR   type=Char label="Planned Duration of Element"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | SCRN | Screening | Informed consent | P14D
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | TRT | Treatment | First dose |
